{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/Kuvvius/status/2098041175974568126","id":"2098041175974568126","text":"GPT-6 Astra did not solve embodied tasks. But it suggests a more consequential possibility: robotics may inherit the scaling curve of general intelligence. (Embodied intelligence as a downstream capability, perhaps.)\n\nThe model that eventually gets us there may not begin as a specialized robot model. It may be a general-purpose model that becomes intelligent enough to understand the physical world, reason about action, and translate its decisions into closed-loop control of a physical body.\n\nCould a robot body become just another interface for a general agent? Like a computer, only much harder. Astra points in exactly this direction, making agentic robotics feel far more promising.\n\nFull analysis of how GPT-6 Astra acts through a body: https://x.com/Kuvvius/status/2098038921301311753","raw_text":{"text":"GPT-6 Astra did not solve embodied tasks. But it suggests a more consequential possibility: robotics may inherit the scaling curve of general intelligence. (Embodied intelligence as a downstream capability, perhaps.)\n\nThe model that eventually gets us there may not begin as a specialized robot model. It may be a general-purpose model that becomes intelligent enough to understand the physical world, reason about action, and translate its decisions into closed-loop control of a physical body.\n\nCould a robot body become just another interface for a general agent? Like a computer, only much harder. Astra points in exactly this direction, making agentic robotics feel far more promising.\n\nFull analysis of how GPT-6 Astra acts through a body: https://t.co/Q11RdR8949","display_text_range":[0,769],"facets":[{"type":"bold","indices":[92,156]},{"type":"italic","indices":[157,215]},{"type":"media","indices":[277,300],"id":"2098040647450304512","display":"pic.x.com/2Wg7w6cF3N","original":"https://t.co/2Wg7w6cF3N","replacement":"https://x.com